  "label": "Meme as a form of hate speech",
  "description": "The meme is classified as hateful because it uses the image of a respected figure to justify a hostile or dismissive stance. This relies on the real-world understanding that memes can be vehicles for hate speech, especially when they use identity-based claims to provoke or belittle. The overall intent is to attack based on ethnicity, which is a form of hate speech.",
